exec(open(__file__.rsplit("/",1)[0] + "/_h.py").read())
B("Matthew", """
1|Matthew begins with the family line of Jesus from Abraham through David. An angel tells Joseph in a dream that Mary's child is from the Holy Spirit, and to name him Jesus, for he will save his people from their sins.
2|Wise men from the east follow a star to Bethlehem and give Jesus gifts. Herod tries to kill him, so the family flees to Egypt and later settles in Nazareth.
3|John the Baptist preaches repentance in the desert and baptizes people in the Jordan. Jesus is baptized, the Spirit descends like a dove, and the Father says: this is my beloved Son.
4|Jesus is tempted in the desert for forty days and resists the devil. He begins to preach and calls Peter, Andrew, James and John to follow him.
5|The Sermon on the Mount begins with the Beatitudes. Jesus says you are the salt of the earth and the light of the world. He teaches about anger, lust, oaths, and love for enemies.
6|Jesus teaches about giving to the poor, prayer, and fasting in secret. He gives the Our Father. Do not worry, seek first the kingdom of God.
7|Do not judge. Ask, seek, knock. Enter by the narrow gate. A tree is known by its fruit. The wise man builds his house on the rock.
8|Jesus heals a leper, a centurion's servant, Peter's mother-in-law, and many others. He calms the storm and frees two demon-possessed men.
9|Jesus forgives and heals a paralyzed man, calls Matthew the tax collector, and raises a girl to life. He says the harvest is plentiful but the workers are few.
10|Jesus sends out the twelve apostles with authority to heal and preach. He warns them they will be persecuted and says whoever acknowledges me before others, I will acknowledge before my Father.
11|Jesus answers John's disciples and praises John. He says: come to me, all who are weary and burdened, and I will give you rest.
12|Jesus is Lord of the Sabbath. He heals on the Sabbath. The Pharisees say he drives out demons by the devil. He gives the sign of Jonah.
13|Jesus teaches in parables: the sower, the weeds, the mustard seed, the yeast, the hidden treasure, the pearl and the net. People in Nazareth reject him.
14|John the Baptist is beheaded. Jesus feeds five thousand people with five loaves and two fish. He walks on water and Peter walks to him, then sinks.
15|Jesus says what comes out of a person's heart defiles them, not what goes in. He heals the Canaanite woman's daughter because of her faith and feeds four thousand.
16|The Pharisees ask for a sign. Peter declares: you are the Christ, the Son of the living God. Jesus says: you are Peter, and on this rock I will build my church. He then first announces his passion.
17|The Transfiguration: Jesus shines on the mountain with Moses and Elijah, and the Father says: listen to him. Jesus heals a boy with a demon, and pays the temple tax.
18|Who is the greatest in the kingdom? Whoever becomes like a child. Jesus teaches about leading others astray, the lost sheep, correcting a brother, and forgiving seventy times seven.
19|Jesus teaches about marriage and divorce, and blesses the children. A rich young man walks away sad. It is hard for a rich person to enter the kingdom.
20|The workers in the vineyard are all paid the same. Jesus predicts his passion a third time. James and John ask for places of honor, and Jesus says the greatest must be servant of all. He heals two blind men.
21|Jesus enters Jerusalem on a donkey, cleanses the temple, and curses the fig tree. His authority is challenged. He tells the parable of the two sons and the wicked tenants.
22|The parable of the wedding feast. Jesus answers questions on paying taxes to Caesar and on the resurrection. The greatest commandment: love God, and love your neighbor.
23|Jesus warns people not to follow the example of the scribes and Pharisees, and then pronounces seven woes on them. He laments over Jerusalem.
24|Jesus predicts the destruction of the temple and describes the signs of the end. Be ready, for you do not know the day or the hour.
25|The parables of the ten virgins, the talents, and the final judgment: whatever you did for the least of these, you did for me.
26|The plot to arrest Jesus. A woman anoints him at Bethany. The Last Supper: Jesus gives his body and blood. In Gethsemane he prays. Judas betrays him. Peter denies him three times.
27|Jesus is handed over to Pilate, who condemns him. He is crowned with thorns and crucified. He dies, the veil of the temple is torn, and the earth shakes. He is buried in Joseph of Arimathea's tomb.
28|Jesus is risen. Women find the empty tomb, and an angel tells them. Jesus appears to them and to the eleven. He sends them to make disciples of all nations, and says he is with them always.
""")
B("Mark", """
1|John the Baptist prepares the way. Jesus is baptized, tempted, and calls his first disciples. He drives out a demon and heals Peter's mother-in-law and a leper.
2|Jesus forgives and heals a paralyzed man let down through a roof, calls Levi, and says the Son of Man is Lord of the Sabbath.
3|Jesus heals a man's withered hand and chooses the Twelve. His family thinks he is out of his mind. He says whoever does the will of God is his brother and sister.
4|Jesus teaches in parables from a boat: the sower, the lamp, the seed growing and the mustard seed. He calms a storm.
5|Jesus frees a man with a legion of demons, heals a woman with bleeding who touches his cloak, and raises Jairus's daughter.
6|Jesus is rejected at Nazareth and sends out the Twelve. John the Baptist is beheaded. Jesus feeds five thousand and walks on the sea.
7|Jesus teaches that what comes out of a person defiles, not what goes in. He heals the daughter of a Syrophoenician woman and a deaf man.
8|Jesus feeds four thousand. Peter says: you are the Christ. Jesus foretells his suffering and tells the disciples to take up their cross and follow him.
9|The Transfiguration. Jesus heals a boy with a spirit. He teaches that the first must be last, and warns about causing others to sin.
10|Jesus teaches about divorce, blesses children and talks to the rich man. He predicts his death, and says the Son of Man came to serve and give his life as a ransom. He heals Bartimaeus.
11|Jesus enters Jerusalem on a colt, curses a fig tree, cleanses the temple and teaches about faith and prayer. His authority is questioned.
12|The wicked tenants. Questions about taxes, the resurrection and the greatest commandment. The widow's two small coins.
13|Jesus predicts the temple's destruction and describes what will happen before the end. Be on guard and stay awake.
14|The plot against Jesus. A woman anoints him at Bethany. The Last Supper, Gethsemane, Judas's betrayal, the trial before the Sanhedrin and Peter's denial.
15|Jesus is brought before Pilate, mocked, and crucified. He cries out: my God, my God, why have you forsaken me? He dies, and the centurion says he was truly the Son of God. He is buried.
16|The women find the tomb empty, and a young man says Jesus has risen. In the longer ending, Jesus appears to Mary Magdalene, then to the Eleven, and sends them to preach the gospel to all creation. He ascends to heaven.
""")
B("Luke", """
1|Luke writes an orderly account. Gabriel announces the birth of John to Zechariah and of Jesus to Mary. Mary visits Elizabeth and sings the Magnificat. John is born.
2|Jesus is born in Bethlehem and laid in a manger. Angels tell the shepherds. He is presented in the temple, where Simeon and Anna see him. At twelve he is found in the temple.
3|John the Baptist preaches and baptizes. Jesus is baptized. Luke gives the family line of Jesus back to Adam.
4|Jesus is tempted. He preaches in Nazareth, where he is rejected, and drives out a demon in Capernaum. He heals many people.
5|The miraculous catch of fish and the call of Simon Peter. Jesus heals a leper and a paralytic, calls Levi, and says he has come to call sinners.
6|Jesus heals on the Sabbath, chooses the Twelve, and gives the Sermon on the Plain: blessed are the poor, love your enemies, do not judge.
7|Jesus heals the centurion's servant, raises the widow's son at Nain, and answers John's disciples. A sinful woman anoints his feet and he forgives her.
8|The parable of the sower. Jesus calms the storm, frees the man with Legion, heals the woman with bleeding and raises Jairus's daughter.
9|Jesus sends out the Twelve, feeds five thousand, and Peter says: you are the Christ of God. The Transfiguration. Jesus sets his face toward Jerusalem.
10|Jesus sends out seventy-two disciples. The parable of the Good Samaritan. Jesus visits Martha and Mary: Mary has chosen the better part.
11|Jesus teaches the Our Father, to ask and receive, and responds to critics. He denounces the Pharisees and scribes.
12|Jesus warns against hypocrisy and greed, and tells the parable of the rich fool. Do not worry. Be ready like servants waiting for their master.
13|Repent or perish. The barren fig tree. A crippled woman is healed on the Sabbath. The narrow door. Jesus laments over Jerusalem.
14|Jesus heals a man on the Sabbath, teaches about humility at meals, and tells the parable of the great banquet. The cost of discipleship.
15|The lost sheep, the lost coin and the lost son, also called the Prodigal Son, show God's joy over a repentant sinner.
16|The parable of the dishonest manager. You cannot serve God and money. The rich man and Lazarus.
17|Jesus teaches about sin, forgiveness and faith. Ten lepers are healed, and only one, a Samaritan, returns to give thanks. The coming of the kingdom.
18|The persistent widow, the Pharisee and tax collector, and Jesus blessing the children. The rich ruler. The third prediction of the passion. Jesus heals a blind beggar.
19|Jesus visits Zacchaeus the tax collector. The parable of the ten minas. Jesus enters Jerusalem and weeps over it, then cleanses the temple.
20|Jesus' authority is challenged. The wicked tenants. Questions about taxes and the resurrection, and about whose son the Christ is.
21|The widow's two small coins. Jesus predicts the destruction of the temple and signs of the end. Be alert and pray.
22|The plot, the Last Supper, and the institution of the Eucharist. In Gethsemane Jesus sweats blood. He is arrested, and Peter denies him.
23|Jesus is tried before Pilate and Herod, and sentenced. He is crucified between two criminals, and says: Father, forgive them. He tells the good thief: today you will be with me in Paradise. He dies and is buried.
24|The women find the tomb empty. Jesus appears to two disciples on the road to Emmaus and is recognized in the breaking of bread. He appears to the Eleven, opens their minds to the Scriptures, and ascends.
""")
B("John", """
1|In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with God, and the Word was God. The Word became flesh and dwelt among us. John the Baptist points to Jesus as the Lamb of God. The first disciples follow him.
2|Jesus turns water into wine at Cana. He cleanses the temple and says: destroy this temple, and in three days I will raise it up.
3|Jesus talks with Nicodemus about being born again. For God so loved the world that he gave his only Son. John the Baptist says Jesus must increase and he must decrease.
4|Jesus meets a Samaritan woman at a well and tells her about living water. Many Samaritans believe. He heals an official's son.
5|Jesus heals a man at the pool of Bethesda on the Sabbath. He says that the Father has given all judgment to the Son. The works and Scripture testify about him.
6|Jesus feeds five thousand and walks on the sea. The Bread of Life discourse: I am the bread of life. Many disciples leave, and Peter says: you have the words of eternal life.
7|At the Feast of Tabernacles, Jesus teaches in the temple. He says: if anyone thirsts, let him come to me and drink. People are divided about him.
8|The woman caught in adultery: let him who is without sin cast the first stone. Jesus says: I am the light of the world. Before Abraham was, I am.
9|Jesus heals a man born blind, and the Pharisees question the man and his parents. The man believes. Jesus says the Pharisees are blind in their sin.
10|I am the Good Shepherd. The sheep hear my voice. I and the Father are one. Some try to stone him.
11|Jesus raises Lazarus from the dead. I am the resurrection and the life. Jesus wept. The Sanhedrin plans to kill Jesus.
12|Mary anoints Jesus at Bethany. Jesus enters Jerusalem on a donkey. Unless a grain of wheat falls into the ground and dies, it remains alone. Many do not believe in him.
13|At the Last Supper Jesus washes the disciples' feet. He says one of them will betray him, and gives a new commandment: love one another as I have loved you. He predicts Peter's denial.
14|I am the way, the truth and the life. Whoever has seen me has seen the Father. Jesus promises the Holy Spirit and gives his peace.
15|I am the true vine and you are the branches. Remain in my love. No one has greater love than this, to lay down his life for his friends. The world will hate you.
16|Jesus tells the disciples about the Spirit of truth, who will guide them. Their sorrow will turn into joy. In the world you will have trouble, but take heart, I have overcome the world.
17|Jesus' prayer to the Father: that his disciples may be one, that they may be kept in truth, and that they may share his glory.
18|Jesus is arrested in the garden. Peter denies him. Jesus is questioned by Annas and Caiaphas and brought to Pilate, who asks: what is truth?
19|Pilate has Jesus scourged and sentences him. Jesus carries his cross and is crucified. He gives Mary to the beloved disciple. He says: it is finished. His side is pierced, and he is buried.
20|Mary Magdalene finds the tomb empty. Jesus appears to her, to the disciples, and to Thomas, who says: my Lord and my God. John says these things are written so that you may believe.
21|Jesus appears to the disciples at the Sea of Tiberias, and there is a miraculous catch of fish. He asks Peter three times: do you love me? Feed my sheep.
""")
B("Acts", """
1|Jesus appears to the apostles for forty days and tells them to wait for the Holy Spirit. He ascends into heaven. Matthias is chosen to replace Judas.
2|On Pentecost the Holy Spirit comes on the apostles as tongues of fire, and they speak in other languages. Peter preaches, and about three thousand are baptized. The first Christians share everything.
3|Peter and John heal a lame beggar at the temple gate. Peter preaches to the crowd in Solomon's Portico.
4|Peter and John are arrested and told to stop preaching. They say: we cannot help speaking about what we have seen and heard. The believers pray and share their goods.
5|Ananias and Sapphira lie to the Spirit and die. The apostles heal many and are arrested, but an angel frees them. Gamaliel advises caution.
6|Seven men, including Stephen, are chosen to serve the widows. Stephen is accused of blasphemy.
7|Stephen's speech traces Israel's history and accuses the leaders of resisting the Spirit. He is stoned to death, and prays for his killers. Saul approves.
8|Persecution scatters the church. Philip preaches in Samaria. Simon the magician tries to buy the Spirit's power. Philip baptizes the Ethiopian official.
9|Saul meets Jesus on the road to Damascus and is blinded. Ananias baptizes him, and he begins to preach. Peter heals Aeneas and raises Tabitha.
10|Cornelius, a Roman centurion, has a vision. Peter has a vision of unclean animals, and goes to Cornelius's house. The Holy Spirit falls on the Gentiles, and they are baptized.
11|Peter explains to the church in Jerusalem why he baptized Gentiles. The church in Antioch grows, and the disciples are first called Christians there.
12|Herod kills James and arrests Peter. An angel frees Peter from prison, and Herod dies.
13|Barnabas and Saul are sent out from Antioch. They preach in Cyprus and Pisidian Antioch. Paul preaches in the synagogue, and the Gentiles rejoice.
14|Paul and Barnabas preach in Iconium and Lystra. Paul heals a crippled man and is stoned. They return and appoint elders.
15|The Council of Jerusalem decides that Gentile Christians do not need to be circumcised. Paul and Barnabas disagree and separate.
16|Paul takes Timothy with him. He has a vision of a man from Macedonia. Lydia is baptized in Philippi. Paul and Silas are jailed, and the jailer and his family are baptized.
17|Paul preaches in Thessalonica, Berea and Athens. At the Areopagus he speaks about the unknown god and the resurrection.
18|Paul stays in Corinth with Aquila and Priscilla for eighteen months. Apollos preaches in Ephesus.
19|Paul preaches in Ephesus, and many believe. The sons of Sceva fail to cast out a demon. A riot starts about the goddess Artemis.
20|Paul travels through Macedonia and Greece. In Troas, Eutychus falls from a window and Paul raises him. Paul says goodbye to the Ephesian elders: it is more blessed to give than to receive.
21|Paul goes to Jerusalem despite warnings from prophets. He is seized in the temple by a mob and arrested.
22|Paul tells the crowd about his conversion and says he was sent to the Gentiles. The mob calls for his death. He says he is a Roman citizen.
23|Paul speaks to the Sanhedrin, dividing Pharisees and Sadducees. A plot to kill him is discovered, and he is sent to Caesarea.
24|Paul is accused before Governor Felix. He defends himself and is held for two years.
25|Festus becomes governor. Paul appeals to Caesar. King Agrippa is introduced to the case.
26|Paul tells his story to Agrippa and says he was not disobedient to the heavenly vision. Agrippa says Paul could have been freed if he had not appealed.
27|Paul sails for Rome. A great storm hits the ship and an angel tells Paul that all will be saved. The ship runs aground at Malta.
28|On Malta Paul survives a snakebite and heals people. He reaches Rome and preaches there under house arrest for two years.
""")
